  "title": "Uniform rules on the native map",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Uniform rules on the native map (computed exactly on the 191 saved and 86 fresh maps). Five uniform canonical rules read the atoms of: yes/no two-stage twins 219 of 277 spaces; native row twins 234; maximal twin cliques 234, since the native twin relation is an equivalence in every space; native twins vetoed by pair refinement 234, since twinship is preserved by refinement and the veto never fires; native twins compatible at glue lines 234. Where the native twins fail they merge atoms (38 spaces), in 32 of them joining two whole atoms by complete twinship. A regularity: two lines of one atom that are native row twins never both create at a glue line with different order-free vectors (17,494 of 17,494 pairs), while across atoms 530 of 1,572 such pairs do, too few to separate every merge.",
